<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Pulseboard — a light issue tracker' }) %>
<%- include('partials/app-shell', { active: '' }) %>

<main class="wrap narrow">
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Track the work, <span class="gradient-text">not the tool</span>.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Projects, issues and a board you can drag — without the forty screens of
      configuration. Everything you have open is one click away: what is assigned
      to you, what you looked at last, what you starred.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <% if (user) { %>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/for-you">Go to your work →</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/projects">Your projects</a>
      <% } else { %>
        <form method="post" action="/demo-signin">
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Open the demo workspace →</button>
        </form>
        <a class="btn" href="/signup">Create an account</a>
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <div class="chips">
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-1)">Projects &amp; issues</span>
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-2)">Drag board</span>
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-3)">Backlog</span>
      <span class="chip" style="--chip-hue: var(--hue-4)">Dashboards</span>
    </div>
    <p class="hint" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      The demo workspace is already populated: two projects, a fortnight of issues
      and a conversation on one of them. No signup to look around.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-label">What is actually hard here</p>
    <h2>Two people change the same thing at the same moment.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      A tracker is mostly forms. The parts that are not are the ones where two
      people collide, and they need different answers — which is the interesting
      bit.
    </p>

    <div class="split" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⇅</div>
        <h3>Fractional ordering</h3>
        <p>An issue's place in a column is a string, not an integer, so a drag rewrites one row instead of renumbering the column.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⚔</div>
        <h3>Version guards</h3>
        <p>A stale drag or edit is rejected with the authoritative issue, and the optimistic UI snaps back instead of undoing someone else's work.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">#</div>
        <h3>Issue numbers</h3>
        <p>PAY-14 must exist exactly once, so the counter lives on the project row and increments inside the insert — not <code>max()+1</code>, which races.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-icon">⌫</div>
        <h3>Delete vs dismiss</h3>
        <p>Removing something from Recent is not deleting it. One × that sometimes destroys your work would be the worst of both.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 18px;">
      <a href="https://github.com/<%= process.env.GITHUB_REPO || '0211IkeVenLouie/pulseboard' %>#the-hard-part">Read the full write-up →</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="site wrap"><span class="faint">Pulseboard · Node, Postgres</span></footer>
</body>
</html>
